#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:3
#: 8ed0d56cbeed42738793b7663ccc4bed
msgid "How to take screenshots and set a wallpaper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:5
#: c313f0014e614ed6857d406fbd9ea3e5
msgid ""
"In Qubes OS, :term:`dom0` is strongly isolated from the outside world. It "
"has no direct internet connection (for updates, a dedicated UpdateProxy is "
"used to avoid interacting with untrusted data) and copying files into it is "
"highly discouraged and not supported by tools such as ``qvm-copy``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:7
#: 9e9f4a9be6924b22b69bcffe7925877c
msgid ""
":term:`dom0` is also where the desktop environment and Qubes OS GUI tools "
"are running (unless you are using the experimental :doc:`sys-gui</user/"
"advanced-topics/gui-domain>`). Thus, if you take a screenshot or want to set "
"a wallpaper, you will be acting within :term:`dom0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:11
#: 9ba7505636014e8a87498f487f0005ed
msgid "Taking screenshots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:13
#: 014ad9c7fd0e42d9be1f04c5c4df126e
msgid ""
"In default Qubes OS installation, you can use the default XFCE screenshot "
"tool (called Screenshot), either running it from the Qubes OS menu or using "
"the :kbd:`PrintScreen` key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:15
#: cba8bb5bbb464840ba0522b926b93297
msgid ""
"image of Qubes Menu with the page for Other tools open and the Screenshot "
"tool highlighted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:21
#: 254e27cdff604c2f87a5646bffaa0b82
msgid "image of the default XFCE screenshot tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:25
#: f851634d73fc4cf3a378143447cd2725
msgid ""
"The file will be saved in :term:`dom0`, so you need to copy it out of :term:"
"`dom0` if you want to use it in any other qube. The easiest way to do it is "
"with the ``qvm-copy-to-vm`` tool in :term:`dom0` terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:31
#: adaa1bcf108940ae9d3ae50760393ee3
msgid "Copying files out of :term:`dom0` is generally safe for your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:34
#: 1306f7745a7540aa9edec3e7ff7472ab
msgid "Setting a wallpaper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:36
#: e2e202d8a8fc42c6b600aca667b248de
msgid ""
"As mentioned, all desktop environment tools run in :term:`dom0`, and copying "
"files into :term:`dom0` is a big security risk and strongly discouraged. New "
"users often ask: fine, :term:`dom0` needs to be isolated, but how do I then "
"set my own wallpaper in Qubes OS then? The possible solutions are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:38
#: 90eaf4572a444ea99cbdc1db5a7fc606
msgid ""
"copy a file into :term:`dom0` in a hacky way (not recommended: this breaks "
"isolation of :term:`dom0` and exposes you to risks from a contaminated "
"graphics file)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:40
#: 85b44acf791344bd80b43db0d3433807
msgid "use screenshots:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:41
#: 0cda04dba4534645a6a5c682cb52578d
msgid ""
"first, display an image you want in **full screen** (you can force full "
"screen by right-clicking on the window title bar, see :doc:`how-to-enter-"
"fullscreen-mode` for more information)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:42
#: 113347bd900d4feaa5926fb8c92d94ad
msgid ""
"take a screenshot (as above, :ref:`take a screenshot <user/how-to-guides/how-"
"to-set-a-wallpaper:Taking screenshots>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:43
#: 7cef3569440541198cc5ee6de88c6180
msgid "use this image as your wallpaper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:45
#: 2944db436e6d4f3eb877f7c27cde9044
msgid ""
"To set a wallpaper in the default XFCE desktop environment, you can use the "
"Desktop tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:47
#: 9ae1250910b745e2a52305d1aba82d0b
msgid ""
"image of Qubes Menu with the page for System Settings tools open and the "
"Desktop application highlighted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-set-a-wallpaper.rst:51
#: 4dded2c8d40d42f59dfe3168323b63d8
msgid ""
"Setting an image as wallpaper **within a normal qube** does not influence :"
"term:`dom0` wallpaper (the one you actually see on the screen) in any way."
msgstr ""
